---

---

<section
  id="no-creeping-margins"
  class="py-20 bg-white relative overflow-hidden border-b border-slate-200"
>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-16">
      <div
        class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 px-3.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#EBF5E9] text-[#469B26] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4 border border-[#bbf7cb]"
      >
        <svg
          class="w-4 h-4"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        >
          <path
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
            stroke-width="2"
            d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"
          ></path>
        </svg>
        <span>The Fleet Fuels Integrity Standard</span>
      </div>
      <h2
        class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-[#2D3136] tracking-tight"
      >
        No Creeping Margins. <br />
        <span class="text-[#469B26]">No Weekly Negotiations.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        We tackle the single biggest frustration in the UK fuel card industry:
        the hidden margin trap. Here is how Fleet Fuels does business
        differently.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Side-by-Side Comparison Matrix -->
    <div
      class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-stretch max-w-5xl mx-auto"
    >
      <!-- The Other Guys (Red/Grey Card) -->
      <div
        class="rounded-3xl p-8 border-2 border-red-200 bg-red-50/30 flex flex-col justify-between relative shadow-sm"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-red-100 text-red-700 uppercase tracking-wider"
            >
              The Common Industry Reality
            </span>
            <span class="text-2xl">❌</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-2">
            Other Fuel Card Providers
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mb-6">
            How traditional brokers treat small and medium businesses:
          </p>

          <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-bold mr-3 mt-0.5">✕</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-slate-900 block"
                  >Teaser Introductory Rates:</strong
                >
                They win your account with an unrealistically low price for the first
                3 to 4 weeks.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-bold mr-3 mt-0.5">✕</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-slate-900 block"
                  >Quiet Margin Inflation ("Creeping"):</strong
                >
                Once your cards are in drivers' hands, their profit margin quietly
                climbs penny by penny.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-bold mr-3 mt-0.5">✕</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-slate-900 block"
                  >Weekly Phone Haggling:</strong
                >
                You're forced to call your account rep every Friday to complain and
                claw back fair prices.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 font-bold mr-3 mt-0.5">✕</span>
              <div>
                <strong class="text-slate-900 block"
                  >Small Fleet Penalties:</strong
                >
                Unless you run 50+ HGVs, you're treated like a secondary priority
                and charged higher rates.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div
          class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-red-200/80 text-xs font-semibold text-red-800"
        >
          Result: Constant administrative hassle, mistrust, and rising fuel
          expenditure.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Fleet Fuels Way (Green Card) -->
      <div
        class="rounded-3xl p-8 border-2 border-[#469B26] bg-[#EBF5E9]/30 flex flex-col justify-between relative shadow-lg"
      >
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
            <span
              class="px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold bg-[#469B26] text-white uppercase tracking-wider"
            >
              The Fleet Fuels Standard
            </span>
            <span class="text-2xl">✅</span>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#2D3136] mb-2">
            The Fleet Fuels Promise
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mb-6">
            Transparent pricing from day one, regardless of your fleet size:
          </p>

          <ul class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-800">
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-[#469B26] font-black mr-3 mt-0.5 text-base"
                >✓</span
              >
              <div>
                <strong class="text-[#2D3136] block"
                  >Fixed Transparent Wholesale Margins:</strong
                >
                The competitive wholesale rate structure we agree on day one is the
                structure you keep.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-[#469B26] font-black mr-3 mt-0.5 text-base"
                >✓</span
              >
              <div>
                <strong class="text-[#2D3136] block"
                  >Zero Creeping Margins Guarantee:</strong
                >
                We never quietly inflate margins down the road. No surprise invoices,
                ever.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-[#469B26] font-black mr-3 mt-0.5 text-base"
                >✓</span
              >
              <div>
                <strong class="text-[#2D3136] block"
                  >No Weekly Negotiations:</strong
                >
                Stop wasting valuable hours every Friday calling to check your price.
                Your rates stay fair automatically.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start">
              <span class="text-[#469B26] font-black mr-3 mt-0.5 text-base"
                >✓</span
              >
              <div>
                <strong class="text-[#2D3136] block"
                  >Big Fleet Prices for Every Business:</strong
                >
                Whether you run 1 van or 30 artics, you access commercial wholesale
                prices previously reserved for conglomerates.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div
          class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-[#469B26]/30 flex items-center justify-between"
        >
          <div class="text-xs font-bold text-[#2c6319]">
            Result: Predictable cash flow, total peace of mind, and genuine
            partnership.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Bottom Quote Box -->
    <div
      class="mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-slate-200 max-w-3xl mx-auto shadow-xs text-center"
    >
      <blockquote
        class="text-sm sm:text-base font-semibold text-[#2D3136] italic"
      >
        "We're not interested in winning your business with a short-term teaser
        rate and then quietly increasing your costs. We build long-term
        relationships based on honesty, transparency, and reliable pricing."
      </blockquote>
      <div class="mt-2 text-xs font-bold text-[#469B26]">
        Gary — Owner, Fleet Fuels UK
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
